      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<br /><img src=\"https://aywren.com/2026/pic/bedlamcoverpt1.jpg\" /><br />\nWhile I’ve only been making YouTube videos for a little over two months, my ambitions always seem to get the best of me. I noticed that my videos seem to get more traction and comments (I’ll write a post about this later) than a lot of my written content does, sadly. So, that got me to thinking about how I might be able to repurpose some of my fantasy stories in an audio format.\n <p>",
